# --------------------- gwt mst options ---------------------

block options
name save_flows
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname save calculated flows to budget file
description REPLACE save_flows {'{#1}': 'MST'}

block options
name first_order_decay
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
mf6internal order1_decay
longname activate first-order decay
description is a text keyword to indicate that first-order decay will occur.  Use of this keyword requires that DECAY and DECAY\_SORBED (if sorption is active) are specified in the GRIDDATA block.

block options
name zero_order_decay
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
mf6internal order0_decay
longname activate zero-order decay
description is a text keyword to indicate that zero-order decay will occur.  Use of this keyword requires that DECAY and DECAY\_SORBED (if sorption is active) are specified in the GRIDDATA block.

block options
name sorption
type string
valid linear freundlich langmuir
reader urword
optional true
longname activate sorption
description is a text keyword to indicate that sorption will be activated.  Valid sorption options include LINEAR, FREUNDLICH, and LANGMUIR.  Use of this keyword requires that BULK\_DENSITY and DISTCOEF are specified in the GRIDDATA block.  If sorption is specified as FREUNDLICH or LANGMUIR then SP2 is also required in the GRIDDATA block.

block options
name legacy_storage
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
deprecated 6.9.0
longname use the storage formulation of earlier versions
description is a text keyword to indicate that the storage formulation of versions of MODFLOW 6 before 6.9.0 will be used.  By default, solute that stays behind when a cell drains is held out of the mobile domain as stranded mass until the cell rewets, instead of being returned to the water that remains.  Two quantities are held back: the solute in the water retained against drainage, whose volume follows from POROSITY and the specific yield of the Storage (STO) Package rather than from user input and is zero unless the specific yield is the smaller, and the sorbed mass.  Solute that a sink carrying no solute leaves behind, such as evapotranspiration given a mixed (AUXMIXED) concentration in the Source and Sink Mixing (SSM) Package, is deposited in proportion to the drained part of the cell, one minus the saturation, and returned as the cell rewets and as recharge from the Recharge (RCH) Package flushes the drained part of the cell.  Stranded mass decays at the rates given for the aqueous and sorbed phases and is written to a binary array file with the STRANDED FILEOUT option.  With LEGACY\_STORAGE, the solute of the drained part of a cell is returned to the water that remains, so the solute mass of a cell whose specific yield is less than its porosity is not conserved as the water table falls and rises.  The earlier formulation is also used, without this keyword, in a model with the Unsaturated Zone Transport (UZT) Package.  When flows are read from a budget file, a time step without storage flow is taken as steady, so a transient flow model must save its storage flows with SAVE\_FLOWS for the drainage of its cells to be represented.  When flows are read from a budget file, the saturation at the start of the first time step is reconstructed from the STO-SY term with the specific yield taken as POROSITY, so sorbed mass is stranded during the first time step but no solute is held back from water retained against drainage.  This keyword is deprecated and will be removed in a future release.
mf6internal ilegacy

block options
name stranded_filerecord
type record stranded fileout strandedfile
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description
mf6internal stranded_rec

block options
name stranded
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname stranded keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to stranded mass.

block options
name strandedfile
type string
preserve_case true
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged false
optional false
longname file keyword
description name of the binary output file to write stranded mass information.  Writing this file is the way to obtain the stranded mass of a single cell over time; like the sorbate concentration, stranded mass is not available through the Observation (OBS) utility.

block options
name stranded_aq_filerecord
type record stranded_aq fileout strandedaqfile
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description
mf6internal strandaq_rec

block options
name stranded_aq
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname stranded_aq keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to the aqueous stranded mass.

block options
name strandedaqfile
type string
preserve_case true
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged false
optional false
longname file keyword
description name of the binary output file to write the aqueous stranded mass of each cell.  The file can be used to give STRANDED\_AQUEOUS for a simulation that continues from this one.

block options
name stranded_srb_filerecord
type record stranded_srb fileout strandedsrbfile
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description
mf6internal strandsrb_rec

